    "tool_args": {
        "text": "# CoA_TRACK → QC_LIMS_Ao: Code-Level Integration Analysis\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nCoA_TRACK is a **production-ready, focused application** with mature code in specific domains that QC_LIMS_Ao has not yet built. The integration strategy is **cherry-pick, adapt, and elevate** — not a wholesale merge. CoA_TRACK uses Integer IDs and a simpler architecture; QC_LIMS_Ao uses UUIDs, soft deletes, and GMP-first design. Every module taken from CoA_TRACK requires **structural adaptation** to match QC_LIMS_Ao's base patterns.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Models & Database Layer — Directly Adaptable\n\n### 1.1 CoA_TRACK Models That Map 1:1 to QC_LIMS Needs\n\n| CoA_TRACK Model | QC_LIMS Target | Reuse Score | Adaptation Required |\n|-----------------|----------------|-------------|---------------------|\n| `Document` | `CertificateOfAnalysis` | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Change `id: int` → `UUID`, add `sample_id` FK, `specification_id` FK, `digital_signature_hash` |\n| `Parameter` | `TestResult` | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Change `id: int` → `UUID`, add `spec_parameter_id` FK, `complies` boolean, `verified_by` FK |\n| `SpecParameter` | `SpecParameter` | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Change `id: int` → `UUID`, inherit from `BaseModel`, add `pharmacopoeia_ref` |\n| `ProductSpec` | `Specification` | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Change `id: int` → `UUID`, add `material_code`, `material_type`, `effective_date`, `expiry_date`, `status` enum |\n| `WaterReport` | `WaterSample` | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Change `id: int` → `UUID`, add `alert_limit_*` / `action_limit_*` fields, `sample_point` enum |\n| `AuditLog` | `AuditEntry` | ⭐⭐⭐ | QC_LIMS has superior `AuditMiddleware` + `audit_log_change()` — merge CoA_TRACK's entity mapping pattern |\n| `Batch` | `Sample` + `Batch` | ⭐⭐⭐ | Split: `Batch` keeps production context; `Sample` gets chain-of-custody fields |\n| `CoQ` | `CertificateOfAnalysis` (CoQ variant) | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Adapt as `CoQ` subclass or status variant of COA |\n| `Embedding` | Qdrant (external) | ⭐⭐ | CoA_TRACK uses pgvector; QC_LIMS uses Qdrant — **logic reusable, storage not** |\n| `User` | `User` | ⭐⭐ | QC_LIMS has superior `Role` enum + passlib; CoA_TRACK has Google OAuth — **merge OAuth** |\n\n### 1.2 Specific Code to Take\n\n**File: `/tmp/CoA_TRACK/app/models.py` lines 96-178 → `Document` model**\n\nThe `Document` model's certificate classification (`cert_type`: icoa | ecoa | coq | water | other), approval status workflow (`draft → analyst_review → qc_approved → issued → superseded → cancelled`), and SOP-aligned sampling points (`SP-01..SP-11`) are **exactly what QC_LIMS needs** for COA lifecycle tracking.\n\n**Adaptation:**\n```python\n# CoA_TRACK Document → QC_LIMS CertificateOfAnalysis\n# Change: int PK → UUID, add BaseModel inheritance\nclass CertificateOfAnalysis(BaseModel):\n    __tablename__ = \"certificates_of_analysis\"\n    \n    coa_number: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(String(30), unique=True, index=True)\n    cert_type: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(String(10), index=True)  # icoa | ecoa | coq | water\n    # ... (rest of Document fields adapted)\n```\n\n**File: `/tmp/CoA_TRACK/app/models.py` lines 181-222 → `Parameter` model**\n\nThe `result_value` (string) + `result_numeric` (float) dual-field pattern is **critical** for preserving raw text like \"<0.1\" or \"n.d.\" while enabling numeric comparison. The `name_local` field for Macedonian names is essential for bilingual compliance.\n\n**File: `/tmp/CoA_TRACK/app/models.py` lines 437-459 → `SpecParameter` model**\n\nDirectly maps to QC_LIMS `SpecParameter`. Add `pharmacopoeia_ref` (e.g., \"Ph. Eur. 2.08.10\") and `sort_order` for display sequencing.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Authentication & Security — Merge Patterns\n\n### 2.1 What QC_LIMS Already Does Better\n\n| Feature | QC_LIMS | CoA_TRACK |\n|---------|---------|-----------|\n| Password hashing | `passlib` (CryptContext) | `bcrypt` direct |\n| Role enum | `Role(StrEnum)` with 6 roles | `role: str` (admin/analyst/viewer) |\n| Token expiry | Config-driven (`settings.access_token_expire_minutes`) | Hardcoded 24h |\n| Soft delete | `is_deleted` on all models | Not implemented |\n| UUID PKs | Yes | No (Integer) |\n\n### 2.2 What CoA_TRACK Has That QC_LIMS Needs\n\n**File: `/tmp/CoA_TRACK/app/routers/auth.py` lines 120-145 → Google OAuth endpoint**\n\nQC_LIMS has **no OAuth integration**. CoA_TRACK's `POST /api/v1/auth/google` endpoint (lines 120-170 in auth.py) verifies Google ID tokens via `httpx` and creates/finds users. This is **directly reusable** for Google Workspace SSO integration.\n\n**File: `/tmp/CoA_TRACK/app/routers/auth.py` lines 34-55 → Pydantic schemas**\n\nThe `LoginRequest`, `UserOut`, `LoginResponse` schemas are more complete than QC_LIMS's current setup. QC_LIMS should adopt the `UserOut` pattern with `avatar_url`, `full_name`.\n\n### 2.3 Recommended Integration\n\n```python\n# In QC_LIMS backend/app/core/security.py — ADD:\n\nasync def authenticate_google(\n    id_token: str, db: AsyncSession\n) -> User | None:\n    \"\"\"Verify Google ID token and return/create user.\"\"\"\n    # Adapt from CoA_TRACK auth.py lines 148-190\n    async with httpx.AsyncClient() as client:\n        resp = await client.get(\n            f\"https://oauth2.googleapis.com/tokeninfo?id_token={id_token}\"\n        )\n    if resp.status_code != 200:\n        return None\n    google_data = resp.json()\n    # ... create or find user by google_sub\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Audit Trail — Merge & Elevate\n\n### 3.1 Current State Comparison\n\n| Feature | QC_LIMS | CoA_TRACK |\n|---------|---------|-----------|\n| Middleware | `AuditMiddleware` (starlette) | None |\n| Service function | `audit_log_change()` | `AuditService.list_entries()` |\n| Entity mapping | None | `_ENTITY_TO_TABLE` / `_TABLE_TO_ENTITY` |\n| Frontend-friendly | No | Yes (maps DB table names → frontend entity types) |\n| Pagination | No | Yes (limit, skip, pages) |\n| Date filtering | No | Yes (date_from, date_to) |\n| User join | No | Yes (joins `User` table for `full_name`) |\n\n### 3.2 Specific Code to Take\n\n**File: `/tmp/CoA_TRACK/app/services/audit_service.py` — Entire file (117 lines)**\n\nThe `AuditService.list_entries()` method with its entity mapping, user join, pagination, and date filtering is **superior to QC_LIMS's current in-memory `_pending_entries` approach**. QC_LIMS should:\n\n1. Keep the `AuditMiddleware` for capturing HTTP-level events\n2. Replace `_pending_entries` with direct database writes using an `AuditEntry` model\n3. Port `AuditService` as `app/services/audit_service.py` with the same interface\n\n**File: `/tmp/CoA_TRACK/app/routers/audit.py` — Entire file (39 lines)**\n\nSimple router exposing `GET /api/v1/audit` with filter params. QC_LIMS doesn't have an audit router yet — this is a **direct template**.\n\n---\n\n## 4. PDF Extraction & AI Pipeline — High-Value Reuse\n\n### 4.1 Extraction Pipeline Architecture\n\nCoA_TRACK has a **mature 3-path extraction pipeline**:\n\n```\nPDF Input\n  ↓\n[Router] Detect PDF type (text vs scanned vs hybrid)\n  ↓\n┌─────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────┐\n│ Text PDF        │  │ Scanned PDF     │  │ Hybrid PDF      │\n│ PyMuPDF extract │  │ Kimi K2.5 Vision│  │ PyMuPDF + Vision│\n│ → DeepSeek flash│  │ → DeepSeek pro  │  │ → Ensemble merge│\n└─────────────────┘  └─────────────────┘  └─────────────────┘\n```\n\n### 4.2 Specific Code to Take\n\n**File: `/tmp/CoA_TRACK/app/ai/router.py` — AI routing logic**\n\nThe `app/ai/router.py` (32 lines) decides which AI provider to use based on PDF characteristics. QC_LIMS's AI pipeline is in planning — this is **exactly the pattern needed**.\n\n**File: `/tmp/CoA_TRACK/app/ai/fallback.py` — 3-tier resilience**\n\nThe fallback module (117 lines) provides degraded service when AI is unavailable. QC_LIMS needs this for GMP compliance — **AI cannot be a single point of failure**.\n\n**File: `/tmp/CoA_TRACK/app/ai/prompts/extraction.py` — Structured extraction prompts**\n\nThese prompts convert PyMuPDF text into structured JSON parameters. The prompt engineering for Macedonian CoAs is **non-trivial and reusable**.\n\n**File: `/tmp/CoA_TRACK/app/ai/memory.py` — Agent memory management**\n\nManages Letta agent conversation memory and context windows. QC_LIMS needs this for its 5 Letta agents.\n\n### 4.3 Integration Approach\n\n```\nQC_LIMS COA Module\n├── services/\n│   ├── extraction_service.py     ← adapted from CoA_TRACK ai/router.py + ai/fallback.py\n│   ├── pdf_parser.py             ← adapted from CoA_TRACK extraction pipeline\n│   └── ai_resilience.py          ← adapted from CoA_TRACK ai/fallback.py\n├── prompts/\n│   ├── coa_extraction.py         ← taken from CoA_TRACK prompts/extraction.py\n│   └── vision_coa.py             ← taken from CoA_TRACK prompts/vision_coa.py\n└── providers/\n    ├── deepseek.py               ← taken from CoA_TRACK providers/deepseek.py\n    └── moonshot.py               ← taken from CoA_TRACK providers/moonshot.py\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Catalog Import Service — Direct Reuse\n\n### 5.1 The XLSX Parser\n\n**File: `/tmp/CoA_TRACK/app/services/catalog_service.py` — Entire file (208 lines)**\n\nThis is a **remarkable piece of code** — it parses XLSX files using **stdlib only** (`zipfile` + `xml.etree`), with zero external dependencies. It handles:\n\n- Shared strings resolution\n- Cell reference parsing (`A4` → column `A`)\n- THC percentage extraction from text like \"THC - 23%\"\n- Quantity parsing with skip logic for \"-\" blanks\n- Deduplicated strain creation\n- Batch upsert (create or update)\n\n### 5.2 Why QC_LIMS Needs This\n\nQC_LIMS will need to import:\n- Batch catalogs from production\n- Excel-based specification files\n- External lab result spreadsheets\n- Stability study schedules\n\nThe `parse_xlsx()` function is **domain-agnostic** — it can parse any Excel file. The `import_catalog()` function is domain-specific but shows the pattern for **bulk import with progress reporting**.\n\n**Direct reuse with zero changes** for generic XLSX parsing.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Frontend Components — React/TypeScript Assets\n\n### 6.1 Component Inventory from CoA_TRACK\n\n| Component | Purpose | QC_LIMS Reuse |\n|-----------|---------|---------------|\n| `ESignatureModal.tsx` | Digital signature with re-auth + meaning capture | **Direct reuse** — required for QP signing |\n| `PermissionGate.tsx` | RBAC component wrapper | **Direct reuse** — wraps any admin-only UI |\n| `StatusBadge.tsx` | WCAG colorblind-safe status indicators | **Direct reuse** — for all status displays |\n| `SessionTimeoutProvider.tsx` | 5-min warning + auto-logout | **Direct reuse** — Annex 11 §6 requirement |\n| `PdfViewer.tsx` | PDF rendering with highlight regions | **Adapt** — for split-panel extraction review |\n| `CoaStatusTimeline.tsx` | Visual status progression timeline | **Adapt** — for sample lifecycle timeline |\n| `DataTable.tsx` | Sortable, paginated table | **Evaluate** — QC_LIMS may prefer TanStack Table directly |\n| `ConfirmDialog.tsx` | Deletion confirmation with reason | **Direct reuse** — for all destructive actions |\n| `AuditTrail.tsx` | Audit log table with export/print | **Adapt** — narrative audit will extend this |\n| `DragDropUpload.tsx` | File upload with drag-drop | **Direct reuse** — for CoA PDF upload |\n\n### 6.2 Critical Components to Port\n\n**`ESignatureModal.tsx`** — This is the **most valuable frontend component**. It implements:\n- Password re-authentication (2nd factor)\n- Meaning-of-signature capture (per 21 CFR §11.50)\n- Digital signature timestamp\n- WCAG accessibility\n\nQC_LIMS has **no e-signature UI** yet. This component should be ported **as-is** with only style token updates.\n\n**`PermissionGate.tsx`** — Simple but essential:\n```tsx\n<PermissionGate allowedRoles={['admin', 'qc_manager']}>\n  <DeleteButton />\n</PermissionGate>\n```\n\nQC_LIMS's `require_role` backend dependency needs a frontend counterpart — this is it.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Business Logic Services — Adaptation Required\n\n### 7.1 CoaService → CertificateOfAnalysisService\n\n**File: `/tmp/CoA_TRACK/app/services/coa_service.py` — 474 lines**\n\nThis service has **excellent patterns** for status mapping, search with pagination, file validation, and deduplication. Key reusable methods:\n\n| Method | Purpose | QC_LIMS Adaptation |\n|--------|---------|-------------------|\n| `map_status()` / `reverse_status()` | Normalize Excel ↔ DB ↔ frontend status | Reuse for all status enums |\n| `_batch_to_list_item()` / `_batch_to_detail()` | ORM → DTO mapping | Pattern for all list/detail endpoints |\n| `list_coas()` | Search + filter + pagination | Template for all list endpoints |\n| `get_stats()` | Dashboard counts | Template for dashboard widgets |\n| `parse_date()` | ISO date parsing with timezone | Reuse everywhere |\n\n### 7.2 CoQService → Quality Certificate Assembly\n\n**File: `/tmp/CoA_TRACK/app/services/coq_service.py` — 647 lines**\n\nThe Certificate of Quality assembly logic (compiling multiple CoAs into a single CoQ) is **unique to CoA_TRACK** and directly applicable to QC_LIMS's COA Generation Module. It handles:\n\n- Parameter aggregation across multiple source documents\n- Denormalized snapshot storage (frozen at approval — GMP requirement)\n- Compliance status rollup\n- AI-generated compliance narrative (`ai_summary`)\n\n---\n\n## 8. Infrastructure & DevOps — Reusable\n\n### 8.1 Docker Compose Setup\n\n**File: `/tmp/CoA_TRACK/docker-compose.yml`**\n\nCoA_TRACK's Docker Compose (Nginx + FastAPI + PostgreSQL) is a **proven production configuration** on KVM4. QC_LIMS can adapt this by adding:\n- Qdrant service\n- Letta daemon service\n- Redis (for event bus / caching)\n\n### 8.2 Nginx Configuration\n\n**File: `/tmp/CoA_TRACK/nginx/default.conf`**\n\nReverse proxy config with static file serving and API forwarding. **Directly reusable** with path updates.\n\n### 8.3 Database Migration Pattern\n\nCoA_TRACK uses `Base.metadata.create_all()` — no Alembic. QC_LIMS needs Alembic, but CoA_TRACK's **model definitions** serve as the first migration target.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Integration Priority Matrix\n\n| Priority | Module | Effort | Value | Action |\n|----------|--------|--------|-------|--------|\n| **P0** | `Document` + `Parameter` models | Low | Critical | Port to QC_LIMS with UUID adaptation |\n| **P0** | `ESignatureModal.tsx` | Low | Critical | Port frontend component as-is |\n| **P0** | `Auth` (Google OAuth) | Low | High | Add OAuth endpoint to QC_LIMS |\n| **P1** | `AuditService` | Medium | High | Replace in-memory with DB-backed audit |\n| **P1** | `catalog_service.py` (XLSX parser) | Low | High | Copy as utility module |\n| **P1** | `PdfViewer` + extraction pipeline | Medium | High | Adapt for split-panel review |\n| **P2** | `CoaService` patterns | Medium | Medium | Adapt for CertificateOfAnalysisService |\n| **P2** | `CoQService` | Medium | Medium | Port as CoQ assembly module |\n| **P2** | `PermissionGate.tsx` + `StatusBadge.tsx` | Low | Medium | Port UI components |\n| **P3** | AI pipeline (router, fallback, prompts) | High | High | Major integration work for 5 agents |\n| **P3** | `WaterReport` model | Low | Medium | Port as `WaterSample` |\n\n---\n\n## 10. Concrete File Mapping\n\n### Files to Copy (with UUID/structural adaptation)\n\n| Source (CoA_TRACK) | Destination (QC_LIMS) | Notes |\n|-------------------|----------------------|-------|\n| `app/models.py` | `backend/app/models/coa_track_import.py` | Rename classes, adapt to BaseModel |\n| `app/services/audit_service.py` | `backend/app/services/audit_service.py` | Merge with existing audit middleware |\n| `app/services/catalog_service.py` | `backend/app/services/import_service.py` | Generic XLSX/CSV import utility |\n| `app/ai/fallback.py` | `backend/app/ai/fallback.py` | 3-tier AI resilience |\n| `app/ai/memory.py` | `backend/app/ai/memory.py` | Agent memory management |\n| `app/ai/prompts/*.py` | `backend/app/ai/prompts/*.py` | Prompt templates |\n| `app/ai/providers/*.py` | `backend/app/ai/providers/*.py` | LLM provider adapters |\n| `frontend/src/components/ESignatureModal.tsx` | `frontend/src/components/ESignatureModal.tsx` | Port as-is |\n| `frontend/src/components/PermissionGate.tsx` | `frontend/src/components/PermissionGate.tsx` | Port as-is |\n| `frontend/src/components/StatusBadge.tsx` | `frontend/src/components/StatusBadge.tsx` | Port as-is |\n| `frontend/src/components/SessionTimeoutProvider.tsx` | `frontend/src/providers/SessionTimeoutProvider.tsx` | Port as-is |\n| `frontend/src/components/ConfirmDialog.tsx` | `frontend/src/components/ConfirmDialog.tsx` | Port as-is |\n| `frontend/src/components/DragDropUpload.tsx` | `frontend/src/components/DragDropUpload.tsx` | Port as-is |\n| `frontend/src/components/PdfViewer.tsx` | `frontend/src/components/PdfViewer.tsx` | Adapt for split panel |\n| `nginx/default.conf` | `nginx/default.conf` | Update paths |\n| `docker-compose.yml` | `docker-compose.yml` | Add Qdrant + Letta |\n\n---\n\n## 11. Adaptation Checklist\n\nFor every model ported from CoA_TRACK:\n- [ ] Change `id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)` → inherit `BaseModel` (UUID)\n- [ ] Add `is_deleted: Mapped[bool]` (SoftDeleteMixin)\n- [ ] Change `created_at`/`updated_at` to use `server_default=func.now()` (TimestampMixin)\n- [ ] Replace `relationship()` lazy loading with `lazy=\"joined\"` for GMP audit performance\n- [ ] Add `__table_args__` indexes for common query patterns\n- [ ] Add `pharmacopoeia_ref` fields for spec parameters\n- [ ] Rename `name_local` → `name_mk` for consistency with QC_LIMS bilingual pattern\n- [ ] Add `__repr__` methods for debugging\n\nFor every service ported:\n- [ ] Replace `db: AsyncSession` parameter with dependency injection pattern\n- [ ] Add `audit_log_change()` calls after mutating operations\n- [ ] Add `reason_for_change` parameter to all update methods (ALCOA++)\n- [ ] Add bilingual response support (MK/EN)\n\n---\n\n## Conclusion\n\n**CoA_TRACK is a goldmine of production-tested code** for QC_LIMS_Ao, especially in domains where QC_LIMS is still in scaffolding phase:\n\n1. **Models**: `Document`, `Parameter`, `SpecParameter`, `WaterReport` are ready-to-adapt\n2. **Frontend**: `ESignatureModal`, `PermissionGate`, `StatusBadge` are immediately portable\n3. **Services**: `catalog_service.py` (XLSX parsing), `audit_service.py` (audit queries), `coa_service.py` (business logic patterns)\n4. **AI**: Prompts, provider adapters, fallback resilience, memory management\n5. **Infrastructure**: Docker Compose, Nginx config\n\nThe total effort estimate for full integration: **3-4 weeks** following the phased priority matrix above. The highest ROI items (P0) can be completed in **3-5 days** and provide immediate COA ingestion capability to QC_LIMS."
